  "title": "S3: dynamic skill disclosure in shadow: per worker spawn compute the smallest useful skill set (deterministic candidates \u2192 cap), log it as the skill_selection decision next to the static exposure, measure the token delta; exposure unchanged (v2)",
  "spec": "Program brief .orchestrator/roadmap-skills.md P8 (steps 1-4 and 7), P10, P29, P30 (P37 stage 3). Depends on T-0894 (skill telemetry: skills_exposed/skills_used/skill tokens in run context, skill_selection decision rows, skill_scorecard) and T-0867 (skills_registry.candidates(task, role), render(id, level), compact skills with declared triggers/task_classes/tools/requires_context). Facts: exposure today is static (all active registry skills for the role); the context program's promotion.mode() reads per-feature modes from pool.toml; decision_log kind skill_selection exists after S1b.\nDo:\n1. pool.toml: add `[skills] mode = \"shadow\"` (off | shadow | active; dated comment; revert: off) and `max_selected = 3`; promotion.FEATURES gains \"skill_routing\" (table skills, key mode, default shadow) with an evidence loader returning n = skill_selection rows carrying a minimal set (stay until Stage 4 scorecards provide quality deltas).\n2. orchestrator/skill_router.py (new): `select(task, role, cfg=None, history=None) -> {\"candidates\": [...], \"selected\": [ids], \"rejected\": [{\"id\", \"reason\"}], \"reason\", \"tokens_exposed_l0\", \"tokens_selected_l0\", \"tokens_selected_l2\", \"ambiguous\": [ids]}`. Deterministic rules: role-only skills that the role's prompt relies on are mandatory (implement-spec for executors, adversarial-review for review/spec_review, challenge for challenge, memory + orchestrate + resume + write-spec for planner, repo-map/test-gap/trace-callers only when their triggers match, classify/compact-memory only for triage); trigger matches from skills_registry.candidates rank next; cap at max_selected keeping mandatory first; candidates with a single weak trigger match (one keyword) go to \"ambiguous\" (reserved for Jev in Stage 9) and are excluded from selected in shadow; `history` (Stage 4 scorecard rows) is accepted but unused until Stage 4 fills it. Never returns an empty set for a role that has a mandatory skill.\n3. Shadow wiring: in spawn.run_worker and the Codex dispatch path, when [skills] mode is shadow or active (active treated as shadow with a one-time notify warning until Stage 5), call skill_router.select and (a) extend the skill_selection decision row from S1b: candidates = registry ids for the role, deterministic = {\"triggers\": matched per candidate, \"task_class\", \"mandatory\": ids}, selected = the minimal set, rejected = the rest with reasons, extra = {\"tokens_exposed_l0\", \"tokens_selected_l0\", \"tokens_selected_l2\", \"ambiguous\"}, mode = the mode; (b) add skills_selected and skill_tokens_selected_l0/l2 to packet_meta so bus.log_run carries them (bus.py copied keys). Worker exposure stays the static set; nothing in .claude/skills, prompts or AGENTS.md changes.\n4. Recovery signal (P30 skill recovery rate): after completion, compare skills_used (S1b) with skills_selected: a used skill that was not selected is a \"skill_recovery\"; record it in decision_log.outcome for the skill_selection row and count it in skill_scorecard as skill_recovery_rate per role (recoveries / spawns with a selection). Also skill_reduction = 1 - tokens_selected_l0 / tokens_exposed_l0 per role.\n5. `orchestrator scorecard --skills` shows selected-set size avg, skill_reduction and skill_recovery_rate; `--economy` skills block includes them. docs/skill-intelligence/04-routing.md (\u226460 lines): the rules, mandatory table, what shadow logs, what active will do (Stage 5), revert path.\nTests (unittest): tests/test_skill_router.py::test_executor_gets_implement_spec_mandatory_and_nothing_irrelevant, ::test_scout_who_calls_task_selects_trace_callers_not_repo_map, ::test_cap_keeps_mandatory_first, ::test_single_weak_match_goes_to_ambiguous_not_selected, ::test_never_empty_for_roles_with_mandatory; tests/test_spawn.py::test_skill_selection_row_and_meta_in_shadow_without_exposure_change (exposure list identical to mode off; decision row carries selected and rejected); tests/test_skill_scorecard.py::test_skill_recovery_rate_and_reduction. Never quote double-brace placeholder tokens literally. Do not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.\n\nSPEC v2 (2026-09-23 04:30) after spec review T-0909 (request_changes), binding on top of v1:\n- pool.toml: add the keys `mode = \"shadow\"` and `max_selected = 3` to the EXISTING [skills] table (created by the discovery task: trusted_repos, allowed_domains); never declare the table twice.\n- The cap applies to non-mandatory candidates only: mandatory skills for the role are always all selected (planner has four), then up to max_selected further candidates by trigger strength.\n- \"Weak match\" is defined by trigger strength, not by count: strength = number of words in the matched trigger phrase(s) summed over matches; a candidate whose total strength is 1 (a single one-word trigger such as \"impact\") is ambiguous; a multi-word phrase such as \"who calls\" has strength 2 and is a firm match. test_scout_who_calls_task_selects_trace_callers_not_repo_map therefore holds.\n- promotion.collect(): a new `if feature == \"skill_routing\":` branch counts skill_selection decision rows whose mode is shadow or active AND whose reason is not the stage-1 static reason (reason != \"stage1 static\"), so the legacy full-exposure rows are excluded; test tests/test_promotion.py::test_skill_routing_evidence_excludes_static_rows.",
